    {
      "name": "Personal",
      "layout": "blog",
      "cover": "assets/personal/cover.jpg",
      "posts": [
        {
          "title": "Finding Light in the Everyday",
          "date": "2025-11-15",
          "body": "There's something about the way light falls through a window at 4pm in November that makes everything feel cinematic. I've been chasing that quality in my personal work — not the golden hour everyone talks about, but the quiet, honest light that shows up when you're not trying.",
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog1a/1200/800",
              "caption": "Kitchen window, late afternoon",
              "camera": "Fuji X-T5",
              "lens": "35mm f/1.4"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog1b/1200/800",
              "caption": "Shadow study on the fire escape",
              "camera": "Fuji X-T5",
              "lens": "23mm f/1.4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "A Week in Oaxaca",
          "date": "2025-09-03",
          "body": "I went to Oaxaca with no shot list and no plan. Just a camera and a willingness to get lost. That turned out to be exactly what I needed. The colors there don't feel real until you see them in person — and even then, your camera can only get halfway there.",
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog2a/1200/800",
              "caption": "Mercado Benito Juarez",
              "camera": "Fuji X-T5",
              "lens": "23mm f/1.4"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog2b/1200/800",
              "caption": "Street mural in Jalatlaco",
              "camera": "Fuji X-T5",
              "lens": "16mm f/1.4"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog2c/1200/800",
              "caption": "Mezcal sunset",
              "camera": "Fuji X-T5",
              "lens": "35mm f/1.4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Why I Still Shoot Film",
          "date": "2025-06-20",
          "body": "Digital is my workhorse. It pays the bills and it's incredible at what it does. But film forces me to slow down in a way that changes how I see. There's a physicality to loading a roll, advancing the frame, waiting for scans. It reminds me why I picked up a camera in the first place.",
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog3a/1200/800",
              "caption": "Portra 400, Coney Island",
              "camera": "Contax G2",
              "lens": "45mm f/2"
            },
            {
              "src": "https://picsum.photos/seed/blog3b/1200/800",
              "caption": "Tri-X, Central Park",
              "camera": "Leica M6",
              "lens": "35mm f/2"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
